# 0002 — The stack, and what it leaves out on purpose

## Context and problem statement

An agent writes most of the code in this project. Every tool below either makes a mistake impossible (types,
schemas, boundaries), makes it loud (gates, scanners, tests against real services), or keeps the blast radius
small (flags, expand-only migrations, immutable images). Choices are pinned to exact versions and changed through
Renovate PRs. This record lists the choices, the deliberate holds, and the tools that are **not** used, so that an
agent (or a person) does not quietly add them.

## Decision

**Environment and agent.** Nix flake + nix-direnv (Node {{ node_major }}, pnpm 11, just, lefthook), Copier for template
updates, Claude Code pinned in the flake with its bubblewrap/socat sandbox, git, gh, jq, ripgrep, fd. The shell also
carries Postgres 18 (local and test database), dbmate (migrations), Squawk (migration lint), oasdiff (breaking API
changes; from the nixos-unstable input until nixos-26.05 has it), sops + age (secrets), Mailpit (local mail) and k6
(load tests).

**Server.** TypeScript (strict), Hono on `@hono/node-server` with `@hono/zod-openapi` and Zod 4, neverthrow, Pino,
OpenTelemetry, t3-env, ts-reset, tsx. Hono's built-in middleware hardens every response: secure-headers (a CSP with
a per-request nonce), body-limit and csrf on `/api/*`; `streamSSE` serves live updates (`/api/v1/events`).

**Data and backend.** Postgres through Kysely + `pg`, with types generated from the real schema (kysely-codegen,
checked by `just check`). better-auth for accounts and sessions (pinned exactly; every endpoint it exposes is in
`openapi.json`, the rest are disabled). pg-boss for jobs and cron. Resend for email, with React Email templates
(`react-email` + `@react-email/render`; the old `@react-email/components` package is deprecated) and Mailpit
locally. OpenFeature with the flagd provider in in-process mode, flags in `flags/flags.json`. Sentry (`@sentry/node`
11) for errors only: traces stay on OpenTelemetry, so nothing is instrumented twice.

{% if kind == 'web' -%}
**Frontend.** React 19 with TanStack Start (and Router), Vite 8 + `@vitejs/plugin-react`, served by the same Hono
process (one port, one image; `src/infra/web.ts`, `scripts/dev.ts`). Tailwind CSS v4, shadcn/ui components copied
into `src/ui/components/ui` on Base UI, react-aria-components only for hard widgets (the language picker). TanStack
Query and TanStack Form, lucide-react icons, self-hosted fonts (`@fontsource`), Paraglide for translations (its
message-format plugin installed from npm, not a CDN), content-collections + MDX compiled at build time (no runtime
`eval`, so the CSP needs no `unsafe-eval`), schema-dts for JSON-LD, satori + resvg for Open Graph images
(`/api/v1/og`; satori draws SVG, resvg turns it into the PNG that social sites require), web-vitals reported to
the server as OpenTelemetry metrics, and `@sentry/react`.

{% endif -%}
**Quality gates.** Biome; ESLint with typescript-eslint, regexp, Vitest{% if kind == 'web' %}, jsx-a11y (6.10.2, run on ESLint 10 through
`@eslint/compat`; `tests/lint/jsx-a11y.test.ts` proves the rules still fire) and react-hooks{% else %}, jsx-a11y and react-hooks (for the email
templates){% endif %}; ast-grep rules
(including the ban on TanStack Start server functions and server routes: every endpoint stays visible to OpenAPI,
the access matrix and Schemathesis). Vitest with coverage{% if kind == 'web' %} and browser mode for components{% endif %}, fast-check, MSW, Stryker; knip,
jscpd, dependency-cruiser, Playwright + axe{% if kind == 'web' %}, size-limit and Lighthouse CI{% endif %}; commitlint; shellcheck and tests for the
Claude hooks; `--check` generators for `openapi.json`, `.env.example`, `db/schema.sql` and the database types.

**Security and supply chain.** Semgrep, CodeQL, gitleaks, TruffleHog; OSV-Scanner, Grype + cdxgen (SBOM), Socket
Firewall, `npm audit signatures`, dependency-review, Renovate; zizmor and harden-runner; Schemathesis, ZAP baseline,
nuclei; the guard and verify-install hooks and the security-guidance plugin.

**CI/CD.** GitHub Actions with Determinate Nix and FlakeHub Cache; a Dockerfile built with buildx, pushed to GHCR
with provenance, SBOM and build attestations; migrations applied before the new image takes traffic; Copier's weekly
template-update PR.

